# Candidate PII — NEVER COMMIT
# ==========================================
# `public/` is served verbatim by the web server, so anything placed here is
# world-readable with no authentication. Per-candidate records (name, CNIC,
# PMDC number, email, phone) belong in Firestore behind auth + rules.
#
# These files stay on disk for local pipeline work; they are simply never
# tracked. The aggregate files in public/data (cutoffs, trends, seats, policy,
# flat_lookup) hold no personal fields and REMAIN tracked — the app needs them
# and they are genuinely public.
/public/data/induction21_candidates.json
/public/data/candidate_auth_index.json
/public/data/grievance_verification.json
/public/data/candidates_changes.json
/public/data/current_merit.json
/public/data/induction21_joining_status.json
/public/data/induction21_merit_round*.json
/public/data/round1_to_round2_merit_report.json
/public/data/sim_merit_cascade*.json

# Service credentials that bypass every access control. The Supabase
# service_role key lives in .env.local (already ignored above); these patterns
# catch key files that get dropped into the repo by mistake.
**/serviceAccountKey*.json
**/*-adminsdk-*.json
**/*service-role*.json

# Local export/backup artefacts that may contain real records.
/exports/
/backups/

